sh it  as far as I can in the show we have a  man who stabs people in the eye with a  needle which is pretty nasty I just love  stuff like that I'm like still 14 years  old inside but you know the thing that I  always look for and I think the reason  why so many people are here at this at  this convention is you know a fictitious  world that's about something that has  ideas that you can think about so you  just watch a show and walk away it  captures your imagination and it gives  you something to ponder afterwards and I  think hunted has that  because it makes you think about good  and bad and how to do the right thing in  this world where you know we all feel so  small in relation to these huge  corporations whose agendas are opaque  you know they don't advertise what  they're doing and why and their their  their motive is profit it's not  necessarily you know anything good so I  thought those are really interesting  ideas to explore in a show was it  deliberate decisions have a female lead  and hunted it was a deliberate decision  to have a female in the lead I just  think you know a woman in this world is  so much more interesting she's  automatically an underdog it is still a  man's world and gives you all kinds of  layers just from the beginning there's  kind of a lot of similarities in a way I  think between Dana Scully aren't there  and Sam hunter was that something that  was unconscious and was that something  that was one was in your mind when  you're making it yeah i think it was  unconscious I mean I think they're both  really smart capable independent women I  think Sam hunter is far more damaged  than Dana Scully ever was much more  emotionally isolated and harder to get  to and that was the challenge honestly  in the characters that she will not  reveal herself emotionally she has no  best friend and so you had to really  make the audience want to know more  about her because she wouldn't open up  that easily and the central relationship  in her life is with her ex-lover Aiden  Marsh played by adam rayner and even  though she's broken up with him and even  though she doesn't trust him he can see  who she is he has all these insights  into her which he doesn't like because  she wants to to put up this wall and  feel invulnerable and that's why the  relationship continues and why it's  interesting to watch that and by the end  of these eight episodes you'll see a  real progression in that relationship  how difficult was it to find an actress  who could play both sides of that in a  way so and so tough and yet so  vulnerable because I know you did to  have in mind originally didn't you  Gillian Anderson yes yeah no I developed  the show with Gillian for a really long  time and she had a lot of really great  insights into the character and then  when I finally got the green light she  couldn't do it so it was incredibly  difficult to find somebody else who had  that skill set they're just  aren't that many actresses in the world  who look like that who have the  physicality and who have the acting  skill and I saw a lot of great actresses  for this part don't get me wrong but  what Melissa brought to uniquely I  thought was the ability to play this  coldness this sort of remove but also  give you the sense that there's somebody  behind that wall that you want to know  more about and there's this duality and  almost every one of her scenes that she  just does effortlessly which to me is  the secret to the to the part and don't  mentioning gum Gillian Anderson there I  know that we see there's loads of fans  out there for for the x files as well as  for hunted now of course too and there's  loads of them who would love to see  another X Files film what are your  feelings on that no I'm a big believer  in another x-files movie and I've been  sort of campaigning for it you know  publicly and behind the scenes ever  since the last movie i think the last  movie just wasn't the movie that the  cinema going public wanted it was a  little movie sort of a story of the week  kind of movie and i think what people  want is the big alien invasion movie  that was promised and is really sort of  the last chapter of The X Files  mythology so it just seems a shame to me  if it doesn't happen and i think there's  pretty strong creative and commercial  arguments for it what would you like to  see happen in that final film well i  can't say i've spoken to it you know for  years now I've been talking to Chris  Carter about it and we have a lot of  pretty clear ideas about what that story  is but I wouldn't want to spoil a  surprise and what it David and David  Duchovny and Gillian Anderson's thoughts  about it do you know our that everybody  wants to do it it's really it's been a  bit frustrating to be honest it's just  it's the studio having the faith to go  forward with the movie and I think  they're feeling because of the last film  not so confident about a final x-files  film but I have to believe in time the  the creative and commercial arguments  will prevail and how about hunted as  well Queen look forward to more series  of this if you've got the map doubt in  your mind already well I hope so I'll  find out in the next few weeks whether  it'll be another season it's been doing  very well on the BBC and on Cinemax in  the US and it certainly could go for  quite a long time so  fingers across the ideas where you might  take it off to this oh I have so many  ideas but you know the the central  question about who's trying to kill sam  and why we go a long way toward  answering that in these first eight  episodes but we don't actually get to  the end of that story so I I hope in the  season two we will miss under to ask  about strike back and also the Star  Chamber because again more spies and  crime thrillers yes well strike back was  sort of a happy accident I i moved to  london and as soon as I got here there  was a delay starting hunted so I I found  myself with nothing to do and and strike  back came my way and I was like  delighted to do it it was not like  anything I've ever done before it was  just fun it was like my inner teenager  again just you know male fantasy action  type stuff and just you know and and was  really brilliantly executed to I think  the producers and the directors of those  episodes it sit there like movies and  it's been very successful so I'm really  you know happy I got to be part of that  in the beginning Star Chamber is is a  remake I'm hoping to do of a great film  starring Michael Douglas about judges  who take the law into their own hands  they start administering the law of the  way they think it should be handed down  and I have a terrific script this being  the movie business you never know when  it will happen he would you like to see  ideally in cost well I can't talk much  about it but I will tell you that the  the central character is is a woman in  the remake when you come to events like  this comic con do you get to release  your inner geek yeah well it's funny I  was thinking about this and you know  there weren't events like this when I  was a teenager if there had been I would  have gone and I I do understand it  though I understand this kind of  devotion because for me growing up  television and movies were incredibly  important I mean it really gave me a way  of connecting to the world that I  wouldn't have had otherwise it was my  lifeline and so I think it's it's  incredible now that there are these  communities that can come together and  share this experience  and and it's a great opportunity for  people to meet other people that they  have a lot in common with  you

